# Line endings are a property of this project, not of whoever cloned it.
#
# Without this file the decision belongs to each machine's `core.autocrlf`:
# the repository stores LF either way, but a Windows checkout hands the working
# tree CRLF, and an editor configured differently puts CRLF back into a commit
# — at which point a one-line change shows up as the whole file rewritten.
#
# `eol=lf` settles both halves at once. Every text file is LF in the repository
# and LF on disk, on every platform. That is already true here — it is this
# line that keeps it true.
#
# It also matters for one file in particular: THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES is generated
# and then compared against the generator byte for byte. The test normalises
# line endings before comparing, but only because it could not rely on this.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never converted, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
